            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Carolyn"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I agree that it is a great starter. I took an Indian twist with this one--double the curry, some cucumber, some onion, and some golden raisins (this makes it!). I also used half the amount of mayonnaise and substituted the rest with yogurt."
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "2"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "HeartySoy9694"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Half a cup of mayo for 4 eggs? My own rule of thumb is 1/2 T mayo per egg, so the 2 T I would use is only 1/4 of what this recipe calls for. For a wetter salad, 1/4 c of mayo--twice what I use--should definitely be enough. The curry powder is a nice touch which we enjoyed and a change from my usual mustard and caper flavored egg salad. This recipe, however, is way too wet and is going to drip all over the place, sliding right out of the sandwiches. I see many of the folks who ranked this recipe as 4-5 stars altered it. I think the sandwiches also are a lot better with a few leaves of butter lettuce and slices of ripe tomato.",
            "datePublished": "2024-01-30T22:02:24.396Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "WorthyGlass1291"
            },
            "reviewBody": "With some arugula or watercress, a dash of mustard, on toasted bread makes It my favorite",
            "datePublished": "2024-01-31T00:21:10.859Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "2"
