            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "SmartFarro9964"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I think the bread should be buttered before putting the filling on it",
            "datePublished": "2024-01-30T21:10:06.966Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "WannaBeChef"
            },
            "reviewBody": "First I used a homemade coleslaw dressing instead of plain mayo. I used red onion. I didn't have any bread so I made some rolls with pancake mix. Just use a 2 to 1 ratio with milk. (2 cups mix, 1 cup milk.) Kneed the dough, on pancake floured surface. The biscuts were sweet, and it went great with the egg salad. I will make this again!",
            "datePublished": "2008-03-06T13:33:33.043Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "bsuever"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I love this recipe. I'm not sure if it is the type of curry that we used (Penzey's) but my husband and I LOVED this! We did not find it as boring as others but I could see spicing it up a bit. I may try that next time. I did add 1 teaspoon of dried, chopped onions and used 6 eggs instead of 4 like other reviewers had suggested. I may even add an extra egg next time I make it. Fantastic and thanks so much for the great idea! Yum!",
            "datePublished": "2009-11-03T15:34:59.060Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Amber Clarke"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I think curry in an egg sandwich is delicious. I did have to add a few more things though or the curry is very over powering. I added 2 tbsp of green onion, 1 tsp of paprika, s&amp;p and I added cheese and lettuce to the sandwiches.",
            "datePublished": "2008-04-01T08:16:14.820Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Angie"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Good recipe, I think a little plain though. I added dired cilantro to the mixture as well as a srpinkle of nutmeg. Tasted wonderful on toasted wheat bread.",
            "datePublished": "2007-04-04T10:28:02.813Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "3"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "darra"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I love curried egg salad sandwiches but this has too much mayo and not enough seasonings. I use a heaping TBS of mayo along with a 1/8 tsp dijon mustard, a little chopped onion, a sprinkling of celery salt, and pepper, a dash of cayenne and any dried herb I'm craving. If I have celery in the house, delete the celery salt and replace with kosher salt. Hope you like it.",
            "datePublished": "2008-02-19T18:21:05.127Z"
          },
